            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Six-Day War and Occupation</strong><br>\nIn 1967, the Six-Day War led to the Israeli occupation of the West Bank and the Gaza Strip. These areas remain disputed to this day, and their future is a central point in Israeli-Palestinian peace negotiations.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Oslo Accords</strong><br>\nThe Oslo Accords of 1993 and 1995 were an attempt to resolve the conflict and allow self-governance for both peoples. They led to the establishment of the Palestinian Authority, but the peace process stalled in the following years.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Current Situation</strong><br>\nThe effects of the Balfour Declaration are still felt today. The conflict between Israel and Palestine continues, and the search for a just and lasting solution goes on. The history of the Balfour Declaration and its consequences are an essential part of understanding the modern Middle East.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
